The guard census on this tree, taken 2026-11-16 before the census was committed in this change.

Command (from the change root):

  tools/loop/census.sh

Output:

  guards: 94
  closed-patron: 4
  no-case: 72
  no-patron: 90
  unheld: 2

The total the retirement uses is the pair: a guard whose cited item is closed *and* whose refusal phrase appears in
no case body. 2 of 94 guards is 2.1 %, below the 10 % stop rule in `proposal.md`. This change therefore stops with the
census as its deliverable; the retirements belong to `the-unheld-guards-are-retired`, which has nothing to start from
this number.

The patron count was read from the tracker; the two offline counts need no credential. A tracker that cannot be read
is printed as `unread` with its reason, never as zero (`census#anUnreadCountIsNamed`).
